<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="1">

  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="4" Page="1" Title=""/>
      <Text>ExT. Farmland - MidNight</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>It’s dark. Cold. ANNIE PERKINS, 27, shuffles through the darkness, uncertain of every step. Hanging on to her hand, and a half-step back, is her daughter, SAMANTHA, 4, scared, exhausted, and hungry.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie tugs on Sam’s hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>AnniE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(forcefully whispering)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Stay close.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sam shuffles in tight to Annie’s side.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The moon hangs low in the sky. Steam rises from the ground.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>They pass a small wooden shack, half-burned to the ground and reeking of wet wood and rotting meat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>As they pass Annie can see a stack of slowly decomposing bodies lit softly by the full moon. She sees the rotting, limbless body of woman near the top of the pile. Her eyes removed, yet the empty sockets seemingly make direct eye contact as they passed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie quickly shakes Sam’s hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Annie (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Don’t look, honey.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sam uses one of her tiny </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">mittened</Text>
      <Text> hands to cover her eyes as if it were some kind of game. A game they’ve played many times before.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The tree line of a large forest lay directly ahead, ominously silhouetted by the moonlight.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Gathering her strength she presses forward, Sam stutter stepping in an attempt to keep up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>They approach the trees. The terrain instantly becomes littered with rocks and downed branches.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie trips and plants her free hand on the soggy ground.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Regaining control Annie wipes wet leaves from her hand on her thigh. She sighs. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ANNIE (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(defeated)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It wasn’t always like this, Sam.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie slows her stride and feels for branches as she pulls her child into the dark, silent woods.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ANNIE (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>When your father was alive, we’d look forward to camping. This was something we’d do for fun. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie looks down at her feet as she slowly stumbles onto a large rock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She rights herself on top and sighs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ANNIE (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>...To get away from it all...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A twig snaps under Annie’s foot causing Sam to jump in fright. Annie puts her free hand on top of Sam’s to calm her.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>They press forward.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ANNIE (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>In a flash, the world changed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie looks towards the sky. The man in the moon steals a glimpse of the two through the trees.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ANNIE (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s hard to imagine an omniscient, omnipresent god commanding it’s followers to commit such an act.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie looks back at Sam who’s eyes are wide with fear.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ANNIE (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>But here we are.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie kneels down and brushes a twig off Sam’s shoulder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ANNIE (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And that was the reason we were given.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sam, petrified, mumbles something faintly.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Sam</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(whisper)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Momma...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie snaps back to the present moment, she turns and follows Sam’s finger pointing behind Annie.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie rises, mouth agape, she pulls Sam behind her tightly and quickly.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>About twenty feet away, standing on the withering remains of a downed tree is a tall, slender man in his late sixties. He’s wearing a long leather duster that slowly shifts in the midnight air. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He holds a twelve-gage shotgun low across his body.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Beams of moonlight rays give him a ghostly silhouette.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>&gt;&gt;This bit needs some work. I like the distance and the </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">imagry</Text>
      <Text>. But I need a little something before they run in to each other. I think Annie should make Sam hide, then it’ll be clear that the man wouldn’t have seen her. Sam can still run out where she does below.&lt;&lt;</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text></Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>With his bush ranger hat covering the majority of his face, the tip of his nose and slit of a mouth are all Annie can see.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She looks down at the shotgun.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ANNIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(struggling)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">...p...p...pl...please</Text>
      <Text>... </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Her eyes well, she fights through the petrifying fear and grabs Sam’s </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">mittened</Text>
      <Text> little hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sam stays hidden behind her mother.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ANNIE (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(faintly)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">...don’t</Text>
      <Text>...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The man raises his shotgun. Annie starts crying a deep sob, her throat opens to create the most pained deep cry of a woman knowing she’s not long for this world.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie releases Sam’s hand, looks toward the ground and drops to her knees; defeated.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sam comes around the side of Annie, </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">afraid...very</Text>
      <Text> afraid, but more for her mother than for herself.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Sam</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(loudly shrieking)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Momma!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The man lowers his shotgun instantly, in a flash. His stance shifts. Mouth agape.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Man</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(flabbergasted)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">A...child</Text>
      <Text>?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie slowly awakens from her shock, she raises her eyes back to meet his.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MaN (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I... I thought...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie slowly nods.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She wipes her face with an open palm and gives out a labored, surprising laugh.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>AnNIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Her names Sammy.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The man smiles and drops to one knee.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(fondly)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Sammy...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He tips his hat back to reveal his warm yet weathered eyes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MaN (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(to himself)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Well... How do you like that?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The sound of heavy feet emerge from the darkness.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The man stands to attention quickly. He looks towards the direction of the disturbed silence.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie pulls Sam close, presses her eyes closed hard and gulps.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Man (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s too dangerous for you both out here at night.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He reaches out his hand to help Annie to her feet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She looks at his hand just as shockingly as he did Sam.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>It was giant, weathered, and the most unexpected site Annie had ever hoped to see.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MAN (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Come.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Annie slowly reaches out with fevered apprehension.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
  </Content>

